{"id":"49cd84fb97221b46","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-cor-lindelof-metric.md","title":"Separable Metric Spaces Are Lindelöf","display":"cor-lindelof-metric — Separable Metric Spaces Are Lindelöf","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-lindelof-metric","aliases":["58-cor-lindelof-metric"],"display":"cor-lindelof-metric — Separable Metric Spaces Are Lindelöf","depends_on":["[[58-prop-lindelof]]","[[58-df-separable]]","[[58-df-metric-space]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-lindelof-metric"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-lindelof-metric</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-lindelof-metric — Separable Metric Spaces Are Lindelöf"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"29039c5a9838faa3\" href=\"?note=29039c5a9838faa3\" title=\"58-prop-lindelof\">58-prop-lindelof</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e861777307dc3417\" href=\"?note=e861777307dc3417\" title=\"58-df-separable\">58-df-separable</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"58-df-metric-space\">58-df-metric-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X,d)\">\\((X,d)\\)</span> (metric space, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"58-df-metric-space\">58-df-metric-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\)</span> (metric-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"58-df-metric-space\">58-df-metric-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_d=\\{U\\subseteq X:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon&gt;0\\;\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\}\">\\(\\tau_d=\\{U\\subseteq X:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon&gt;0\\;\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\}\\)</span> (metric topology)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Separable}(X,\\tau_d)\">\\(\\operatorname{Separable}(X,\\tau_d)\\)</span> (separability predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"e861777307dc3417\" href=\"?note=e861777307dc3417\" title=\"58-df-separable\">58-df-separable</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Lindelof}_S(X,\\tau_d)\">\\(\\mathrm{Lindelof}_S(X,\\tau_d)\\)</span> (Lindelöf-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"29039c5a9838faa3\" href=\"?note=29039c5a9838faa3\" title=\"58-prop-lindelof\">58-prop-lindelof</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}lindelof\\text{-}metric} \\vdash \\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\tau_d=\\{U\\subseteq X:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\}\\land\\operatorname{Separable}(X,\\tau_d)\\to\\mathrm{Lindelof}_S(X,\\tau_d)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}lindelof\\text{-}metric} \\vdash \\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\tau_d=\\{U\\subseteq X:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\}\\land\\operatorname{Separable}(X,\\tau_d)\\to\\mathrm{Lindelof}_S(X,\\tau_d)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every separable metric space is second countable and therefore Lindelöf. Metric balls are expanded through <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span>, eliminating the free ball operator <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_d\">\\(B_d\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The dependency is the topological Lindelöf predicate, not the unrelated Lindelöf hypothesis for the Riemann zeta function.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-prop-lindelof","status":"resolved","id":"29039c5a9838faa3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-prop-lindelof]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-separable","status":"resolved","id":"e861777307dc3417","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-separable]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-metric-space","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-metric-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-metric-space","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$(X,d)$ (metric space, see [[58-df-metric-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-metric-space","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S$ (metric-space predicate, see [[58-df-metric-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-separable","status":"resolved","id":"e861777307dc3417","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Separable}(X,\\tau_d)$ (separability predicate, see [[58-df-separable]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-prop-lindelof","status":"resolved","id":"29039c5a9838faa3","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Lindelof}_S(X,\\tau_d)$ (Lindelöf-space predicate, see [[58-prop-lindelof]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(X,d)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_d=\\{U\\subseteq X:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon>0\\;\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)<\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Separable}(X,\\tau_d)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Lindelof}_S(X,\\tau_d)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}lindelof\\text{-}metric} \\vdash \\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\tau_d=\\{U\\subseteq X:\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)<\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\}\\land\\operatorname{Separable}(X,\\tau_d)\\to\\mathrm{Lindelof}_S(X,\\tau_d)","display":true},{"tex":"d","display":false},{"tex":"B_d","display":false}],"bytes":1412,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-74","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-cor-lindelof-metric.md|58-cor-lindelof-metric]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["29039c5a9838faa3","e861777307dc3417","ce876585d129ce97"]}